{"availability":"available","full":"EvanZhouDev/ui2","name":"ui2","description":"The Unified Intent Interface: The easiest way to build intent-powered UIs","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":222,"forks":14,"created":"2025-04-17T18:01:45Z","updated":"2026-04-06T04:14:39Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ui2-docs.vercel.app","topics":["intent","ui"],"demo":"https://ui2-docs.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:16.688Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:16.688Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:16.688Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T09:08:16.688Z","stars":222,"forks":14}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["UI2 seeks to directly convert user intention into action. Think if an assistant like Siri was implemented directly into an application—but you can type to it, and due to its deep integration, it's accurate, powerful, and fast.","And not only that, you can see exactly what that assistant would do as you are typing.","Learn more and get started with development at ui2-docs.vercel.app"],"features":["Unification: Search, taking action, and everything else you can do on an application should not be separate interfaces, but rather unified into one.","Intent Detection: The key point in combining these interfaces is identifying the user intent, now possible through LLMs","Context: Not only is intent detection based off of the text that you are typing, it also draws context from everything in your app—Allowing more powerful and more accurate intents.","Instant Preview: Imagine autocomplete for actions—not just words, in which you can \"preview-before-committing.\""],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/EvanZhouDev/ui2/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"26b72b90761a5b9cdbfbd983b30a6e00584625aab5106364390d259659511f8d","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:16.849Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:16.849Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"